WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.260
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.840
<i>I took being there for granted.</i>

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.630
<i>Ever since that day, I felt awkward,</i>
<i>so I didn't wanna see her.</i>

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.970
<i>I thought I was doing a favor.</i>

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.340
<i>She was being a pest.</i>

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.050
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.880
<i>But I was wrong.</i>

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.720
- <i>Yes, I know now.</i>
- <i>I know now.</i>

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.850
<i>I was just getting</i>
<i>accustomed to feeling good.</i>

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.720
<i>I had been leaning on her.</i>

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.800
<i>I never realized.</i>

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.760
<i>I finally realize.</i>

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.570
- <i>My feelings!</i>
- <i>My feelings!</i>

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.400
- <i>For you.</i>
- <i>For you.</i>

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:57.240
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:04.820
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.830
Although loneliness...

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:13.160
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:20.400
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.480
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.450
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:35.980
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:39.760
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.390
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.090
Some light is shed...

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:51.670
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:58.910
...so that we can go to a different place

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:06.910
The things I want have no shape

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:15.320
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.460
In Order to Survive

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.080
I'd been looking at it.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.650
I had always been looking
straight at it, but never knew.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:47.590
Ever since I felt that coarse something.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.800
<i>I've gotta save that person.</i>

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.470
<i>How could you say such a thing?</i>

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.840
<i>What makes you think you're so great?</i>

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.910
<i>Can't you even figure that out? You fool.</i>

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.340
<i>Why don't you just disappear?</i>

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.740
I just... continued... to watch.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:07.610
Yes.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.910
While drifting within a dark world...

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:14.750
...I've continued watching something
as it stirs on the other side.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.960
Various colors would dance within me,
and then vanish.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.300
Various colors, weak, strong...

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.420
...bright, and dark.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.700
Now I know the meaning of those colors.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:35.000
Joy, sorrow, anger, anxiety...

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:38.970
...discontent, pleasure, impatience, hope...

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:42.350
...despair, ambition, passion...

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:46.010
...murderous intent,
enchantment, jealousy...

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.420
...delight, envy, grief, desire.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.860
I strongly felt the souls of people...

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.490
...the strong feelings of people.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:01.830
Soon, I was able to sense the
feelings of many of the people here.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.360
Like the person who believes
there is only one way to survive.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.340
The person who struggles to do something
about a situation that's out of control.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.510
The person who vowed never to
make the same mistake again.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.180
The person who insists on
living true to her feelings.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.720
The person who lives day-to-day...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.060
...unable to put into words the
feelings she locks within her.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:29.500
The person who is denied his way of living,
but continues to push forward.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.020
The person who dislikes anything less
than perfect, and searches for excellence.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.270
The person who believes in her ideals,
and cuts off her past, to live her future.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:42.580
The person who hates to
be held back by his past...

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.100
...and continues searching for
the place where he should be.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.110
The various thoughts that mingle
with each other, melt into me...

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.110
...until at some point one clear,
united feeling arises.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.290
That feeling...!

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:16.710
I don't want to die.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.840
I want to keep on living.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.750
As simple as that.

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:24.520
However...

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:27.180
...my awakenings would
never come to an end.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.420
I'd be forcefully pushed
by a torrent of emotions...

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.890
...leading me to awaken new powers.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.100
Damn you!

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:41.590
<i>Why? Why does this have to happen?</i>

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.400
<i>Damn! Damn!</i>

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.770
<i>Get real!</i>

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.910
<i>What is it, anyway?</i>

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.540
<i>What did I do to deserve this?</i>

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.900
I'm scared!

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.870
Juli!

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.830
They are depth bombs
coming from ordinary space!

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:40.960
I'm pulled by strong senses,
hiding deep within my emotions.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.860
But I don't want to see you.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.930
But I want to be kind.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.200
But I want to be by your side.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.170
But I want to be near you.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.430
But I want to be connected.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:54.700
All I want is to be with you...!

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:57.900
Then something appears that opposes this.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.810
Someone ends up appearing.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.440
Without even a moment for
us to surrender to grief...

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.480
...quickly... quickly...

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.490
...quickly... quickly...!

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.990
What's this? It's nothing like ours.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.630
It has a drill on it.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.690
- This is the enemy's...!
- Vital Guarder?

00:07:26.310 --> 00:07:27.740
The second wave's coming!

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.280
Final attacking charge!

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.880
CHARGE!!

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.980
Now the enemy Vital
Guarder is coming at us!

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:39.950
Our field won't be enough
to defend against it!

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.560
Ikumi! Hurry!

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.020
<i>I know!</i>

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.020
Vital Guarder won't get here in time!

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:50.100
What?

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.160
I believe the attack's coming
from the enemy Vital Guarder!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.270
Stein's calculations were right on.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.570
But just getting rid of the
rocks may be the best we can do.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:07.580
Take the enemy's field
into consideration!

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:09.240
It'll be 111 seconds before
the next shot's loaded!

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.110
Not quick enough! Give it to me!

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.420
- Marco, set output at 83 percent.
- Gotcha!

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:17.580
The Enemy Vital Guarder will
reach the Ryvius in 158 seconds!

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:20.160
Break apart the SK Solid!
We'll begin developing a field!

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:23.590
Transform it into a tube shape! You should
be able to neutralize and get past it!

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.400
Maximum field developed!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.700
Crush the main ship before the
Vital Guarder has a chance to move!

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:33.300
Countdown till the enemy Vital
Guarder hits the Ryvius... 29, 28...!

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.480
We won't succumb that easily!

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.680
You're the ones...

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.220
...destined to die.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.850
They exist in the same manner that I do.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.960
We're friends.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.060
However, they would not respond,
no matter how I called out to them.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.670
All they'd do is throw
their shade of anger at me.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.370
Cullen! Develop the expansion
field in the direction of the Ryvius!

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.500
Don't blame me, whatever happens.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.310
What's the big idea?

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:15.120
I told you, I'm doing as I wish!

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.280
- You've gotta be outta your mind!
- Stop!

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.660
Are they by chance trying to break
through a crack in the field?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.220
That's too dangerous! Stop them!

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.690
But that's our only chance.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.930
- Now, Yuki!
- I know!

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:51.610
- What is that?
- Disruptions are appearing in the Finafield!

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:56.650
We must protect! No matter what it takes,
we'll protect!

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.330
- Pinger reacting! Got it!
- A separation type?

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.970
Eysfina is docking,
for puppet wire recovery!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.780
Make it stop!
They could target them all with one shot!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.110
- But...!
- If we can't, fire all bullets at once! Hurry!

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.920
Impossible. The percentage
of severed puppet wires is...!

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.290
Then bring back Eysteral!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:35.630
The time you take doing things,
a cat could a better job!

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:37.630
Solid transferred.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.660
Target approaching!
20 seconds before it reaches us!

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.630
Even so...!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:46.140
This will...!

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:47.410
...I...

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:48.640
Finish it off!

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:50.110
...continue to live.

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.390
The Eysteral has been destroyed!

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:04.750
Enemy fire hit main output source!
Unable to navigate!

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.330
Do something!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.320
You're all too young!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:20.200
Towed array... decreasing.

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.840
Gravitational faults are disappearing.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:28.110
Many unmistakable senses
sprout inside me.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:31.410
I want to live.
I want to survive.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:34.710
I don't want to die. I
want to continue laughing.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.820
I don't want sorrow. I love you.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.160
I love you. I love you.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.930
I can't stop these
overflowing feelings for you.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:52.970
I long for you so much.
But what is it that <i>you</i> want to do?

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.670
What are your wishes?

00:11:55.910 --> 00:11:57.880
How do you want to spend your time?

00:12:11.320 --> 00:12:13.450
What do you want to do?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.460
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:23.500
Infinite Ryvius

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.970
The effects of the enormous Neutrino
Burst that occurred 16 hours ago...

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.840
...will reach the vicinity
of Earth at 5:23 p. M.

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.050
At that time, normal communication will
not be possible for about thirty hours.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.990
For emergency communications,
please use the SK circuit.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.650
It must be years since we last
met like this, Shimomura.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:51.300
I didn't come to reminisce
about the good old days.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.200
Actually, I'd like you to.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:56.670
Tell me why you decided
to steal the Bratica...

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.570
...or rather the Ryvius,
12 years ago.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:02.940
Too much power leads to foolish acts.
We must balance power.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:08.100
We have no intention of gaining mastery
through force. I won't take that nonsense.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.780
Then why use Vaia ships?

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:14.220
Almost all of the navigators have been
exposed to a "backyard" from the Sphix...

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.710
...and have shown signs
of mental breakdown.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.730
So you knew about that.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:21.920
I can't believe you people
have any sense of morals.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:25.400
Too much is still unknown about Vaia.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.800
Your actions should be
prudent and justifiable.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.040
Have you noticed that...

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:35.470
...although subtle, the time between
Neutrino Blasts has narrowed?

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.540
What?

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:41.880
When the Second Geduld Phenomenon
takes place in several thousand years...

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.580
...the whole solar system will be destroyed.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.790
The Vaia are necessary in
order for humankind to survive.

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.790
No, in particular, the Ryvius,
is a ship that can continue ordinary flight...

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.230
...on its own for over six months.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.160
Even if you know that children
are aboard that ship?

00:13:58.970 --> 00:14:01.300
These are your internal
documents that I retrieved.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:05.040
The Ryvius is sailing with a few hundred
people aboard, all children.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.070
Vice-Minister!

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.370
I had received notice about
something of the sort...

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.540
...although I could not verify it to be true.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.210
Then we must save the children at once.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.370
- I can't do that!
- What?

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:18.120
Even if that information
proves to be true...

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.880
...we can't afford to miss
this great opportunity.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:25.160
We must do what we can now, so that
we can maintain assets for the future.

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:28.660
The destiny of the solar system
lies with the actions of the Ryvius.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.290
But don't you find this is going too
far against the humanitarian values?

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.660
To sacrifice the lives of all those children?

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:38.300
I realize that what I'm doing is the
worst possible thing a person can do.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.410
However,
unless someone steps forward...

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.580
...and takes drastic actions
to lay the foundation...

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.130
...there will be no future for humankind.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.270
We should be able to deal with the
situation even if we save them.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:51.780
The Solar System Alliance Supreme Council
has already decided on this.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:54.280
H-However...!

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:58.160
Even if the Ryvius' activation was
merely a product of coincidence...

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.230
...as a result, we were able to
get our hands on new hope.

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:04.790
We can't afford to let our immediate
emotions cause that flame to diminish.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:09.670
If it'll result in the Ryvius' true awakening,
no sacrifice is too big.

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.970
I don't care if I must face trial for my actions,
or be reviled until the end of time.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:15.300
I believe I'm prepared to
accept any consequence.

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:20.340
We have an obligation to guide the
people and make a path to the future.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:22.950
Na-na-na, na-na!

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:25.310
Give it back to me.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.150
Will you stop that?

00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.780
Return that bag to the child at once!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.990
Now...!

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.590
Stop it! Stop it!

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:41.990
Stop right there!

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.000
Stop, please! Someone, help me!

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.720
Adjusted to 10 below standard.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.590
Control solids are to be
developed in order.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:05.730
No errors have ben picked up
to this point.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:06.960
Initial stage complete.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:09.160
Vaia Project?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:13.130
In plain words, it's a project to
escape to the outskirts of space...

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:15.030
...with the use of Vaia ships
capable of gravitational control...

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:17.540
...before the solar system is destroyed.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.610
It almost sounds like an idea
a child would come up with.

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.840
So the rumors were true.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:26.510
That creatures living within Geduld are
used as the nucleus of this ship we're on.

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:28.350
That's what a Vaia is.

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:31.020
It is unknown how these
creatures came to be.

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.020
There's a theory that suggests that
just before the Geduld Phenomenon...

00:16:33.020 --> 00:16:36.280
...intelligent life forms came
in contact with the Sun...

00:16:36.990 --> 00:16:39.260
...but none of that's important right now.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.450
Humankind was in need
of an unknown power.

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:43.730
The power of the Vaia.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.220
Are you aware that several
hundreds of thousands of people...

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:51.860
...were sent to capture those Vaias,
existing within Geduld...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.270
...and 80 percent of them died?

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:57.540
But still humankind needed Vaia ships,
for the future that will eventually come...!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.870
We succeeded in building six Vaia ships.

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:03.750
However...

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.120
...all crew members aboard
developed mental disorders...

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.350
...and in addition,
The Ryvius only moved on one occasion.

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.890
So many lives were sacrificed for nothing,
so it seemed.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.300
But six months ago...

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:20.600
...an incident occurred,
leading to the Ryvius' awakening.

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:23.360
- The incident we were involved in.
- Yes, that's right.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.010
It's unknown what caused its
activation the second time.

00:17:27.740 --> 00:17:31.770
But the Ryvius grew stronger after
each battle it was involved in.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:35.910
A ship that could control its gravitational field,
and would not run off on its own.

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.080
Maybe, without even realizing it,
we had developed high expectations for it.

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.020
However...!

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:44.150
Who would've expected that there were
only children aboard the Ryvius.

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:47.060
But no.

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:51.090
After learning about that fact,
I've still given up on those helpless children.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.130
Even though they may have
been influenced by the Sphix.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:17:57.900
I am mistaken.

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:00.740
I know that for a fact. Yet...!

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:05.910
The Neutrino Burst will
arrive in a moment.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.580
There is the risk of it being
harmful to the human body...

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:12.140
...and therefore, people outside are
advised to move indoors at once.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.860
I must fulfill my
responsibilities as an adult.

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:34.840
For the children aboard the Ryvius,
who I don't even know the names of.

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.070
The Vaias are a threat to us all.

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:42.540
Although orders from
above are to capture it...

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.510
...depending on how the other ship reacts,
be forewarned that we may have to destory it.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.980
I'll make sure all
crewmembers are fully aware.

00:18:53.460 --> 00:18:55.720
I've become so damn good at lying.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:58.620
A Vaia being used to capture a Vaia.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.470
That in itself is a contradiction.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:03.700
Don't you think so, Ange?

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.000
Do you realize the extent of losses
we've incurred by losing the Ryvius?

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.200
Why did you try to transport
the Bratica and Vaia separately?

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:36.600
The Sphix hadn't crystallized yet!
Of course it would reject!

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.570
You're responsible for everything!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:41.010
Don't you feel remorse for what
happened to your subordinates?

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.840
How could the father survive
instead of his daughter?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.780
I'll put an end to this,
for your sake as well.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:03.230
There is no Black Ryvius.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.600
It's the Bratica.
It's nothing other than my disgusting past.

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:10.240
I will bury that Bratica.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.330
I live for that reason and that reason only.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.070
I live for that reason only.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.670
<i>This is crazy. Everything has gone crazy.</i>

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.540
<i>But, even with all the</i>
<i>abnormality within the Ryvius...</i>

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.950
<i>... as long as there's someone</i>
<i>that I must protect!</i>

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.620
<i>You hypocrite!</i>

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:35.090
<i>I'm not like you, brother, always doing</i>
<i>as others wish. I act on my own will.</i>

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.150
<i>You guys don't do anything,</i>
<i>yet consistently make claims.</i>

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:41.000
<i>And you actually think you've</i>
<i>accomplished something by doing so.</i>

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.030
<i>I'm not gonna give up on her!</i>

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:47.040
<i>It was my fault. Damn.</i>

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.770
<i>How many times must we repeat this?</i>

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:53.870
<i>Answer me, Kouji! Well, tell me!</i>

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:56.150
Yuki. Ikumi.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.710
I'm beginning to think that what
you guys are saying is correct.

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:02.720
It's as if my feelings, my thoughts,
are being sucked up by the Ryvius.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.320
<i>But Kouji, you're pulled along by Ikumi.</i>

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.090
<i>That's not in your character, Kouji.</i>

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.860
<i>If you try too hard, you'll end up failing.</i>

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:16.590
<i>Guys like you and I are</i>
<i>better off staying quiet.</i>

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:19.660
<i>You can only part with</i>
<i>your past, on your own.</i>

00:21:20.470 --> 00:21:25.340
<i>Is it wrong to think the</i>
<i>way I do here, on the Ryvius?</i>

00:21:26.480 --> 00:21:28.570
<i>Don't try to end a conversation like that.</i>

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:31.180
<i>If you have something you</i>
<i>wanna say, then say it.</i>

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:33.390
<i>Otherwise, how am I supposed to know?</i>

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.650
<i>There's no connection</i>
<i>there, right? Please, Kouji.</i>

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:38.660
<i>Aoi.</i>

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:39.960
<i>Not at all!</i>

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.960
<i>You just need to make a priority list.</i>

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:43.930
<i>You don't have to make any special</i>
<i>effort but make up your mind to do them.</i>

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.530
<i>Just by doing that, you should be</i>
<i>able to overcome almost anything.</i>

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.260
<i>Why can't you be prepared</i>
<i>for the inevitable!</i>

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.870
Be prepared...!

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:58.270
<i>And I'm also interested.</i>
<i>To see how you would use it.</i>

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:11.080
In your dry eyes...

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:16.150
...a silhouette appears

00:22:16.150 --> 00:22:20.850
The blue colored future...

00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:27.590
...swayed and glittered

00:22:28.760 --> 00:22:37.000
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:45.610
...freedom out of pity

00:22:45.610 --> 00:22:54.050
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:57.960
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:57.960 --> 00:23:04.330
goodbye

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:10.320
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:11.660
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: Torn Past
When I first met him...

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.490
Next episode: Torn Past
...I thought he was a great guy.

00:23:13.490 --> 00:23:15.060
Next episode: Torn Past
He understood me...

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.560
Next episode: Torn Past
...and I made an effort to understand him.

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:20.600
Next episode: Torn Past
However, the torn past...

00:23:20.600 --> 00:23:22.400
Next episode: Torn Past
...the traces of sadness...

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:25.000
Next episode: Torn Past
...separate Ikumi from myself.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.340
Next episode: Torn Past
I never believed in friendship...

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:28.570
Next episode: Torn Past
...but still...!
